This document identifies third-party components used by the GenieX SDK, CLI,
and language bindings. GenieX's BSD 3-Clause license applies to its own code;
it does not replace the licenses or agreements governing third-party components.
The original copyright notices, license texts, and component-specific terms
remain authoritative and must be preserved as required when redistributing them.

Dependency versions are recorded in `cli/go.mod`, `sdk/model-manager/Cargo.lock`,
the tokenizers-cpp Cargo lockfile, and the pinned git submodules. Optional,
test-only, build-time, and platform-specific dependencies are not necessarily
included in every runtime distribution.

## Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT)

The open-source [geniex-qairt-plugin](https://github.com/qualcomm/geniex-qairt-plugin)
is BSD-3-Clause, but its QAIRT SDK headers and prebuilt runtime libraries are
**proprietary Qualcomm components governed by the Qualcomm AI Runtime SDK EULA**.
They are not relicensed under GenieX's BSD license. This notice does not grant
rights to redistribute them; follow the EULA supplied with the applicable SDK.

See [the plugin's third-party notices](third-party/geniex-qairt/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)
and `qnn-api/README.md` in that submodule for the SDK/runtime versions and terms.
Other externally supplied Qualcomm SDK components retain their respective
licenses and agreements.

