| webpki-roots (Android only) | CDLA-Permissive-2.0 |
| async-trait, url, fs2, flate2 | MIT OR Apache-2.0 |

The QAIRT plugin's tokenizers-cpp submodule also builds a Rust tokenizer.
Important transitive components from both the model-manager and tokenizers-cpp
lockfiles, and their distinct terms, include:

| Component | License |
| --- | --- |
| ring | Apache-2.0 AND ISC; preserve its BoringSSL and other embedded-code notices |
| rustls-webpki | ISC |
| rustls-pki-types, tokio-rustls | MIT OR Apache-2.0 |
| rustls-native-certs | Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT |
| webpki-root-certs | CDLA-Permissive-2.0 |
| tokenizers | Apache-2.0 |
| onig, onig_sys | MIT for the Rust bindings; the bundled Oniguruma library retains its BSD license |
| ICU4X crates, including icu_locale_core, icu_normalizer, and icu_properties | Unicode-3.0 |
| unicode-ident | (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0 |

The complete resolved graphs, including build, test, and platform dependencies,
are in `sdk/model-manager/Cargo.lock` and
`third-party/geniex-qairt/third-party/geniex-proc/third-party/tokenizers-cpp/rust/Cargo.lock`.
Consult each resolved crate's own license files for its full terms. A license
expression using **AND** requires both sets of terms; **OR** denotes alternatives.

