`bindings/android/app/build.gradle.kts` declares AndroidX core-ktx and Kotlinx
Coroutines Android. The Kotlin standard library and these libraries use
Apache-2.0. Their resolved transitive dependencies retain their own licenses.

| Component | License | Upstream |
| --- | --- | --- |
| AndroidX core-ktx | Apache-2.0 | https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx |
| Kotlin Standard Library | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin |
| Kotlinx Coroutines | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.coroutines |
| LLVM OpenMP runtime (`libomp.so`) | Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; upstream legacy notices also apply | https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/openmp |

`bindings/android/app/extLibs/arm64-v8a/libomp.so` was copied from the Android
NDK and is packaged into the AAR by the binding's Gradle build. Consult the
supplying NDK's `NOTICE.toolchain` and the [OpenMP license](https://android.googlesource.com/toolchain/llvm-project/+/d8003a456d14a3deb8054cdaa529ffbf02d9b262/openmp/LICENSE.TXT)
for the full license text and legacy Intel OpenMP copyright and license notices.

Version-catalog entries alone do not imply that a library is used by the binding.

## Test Assets and Optional Tooling

Test assets have separate attributions in [tests/assets/NOTICE.md](tests/assets/NOTICE.md),
including the CC BY 2.0 image used by VLM quality tests. Optional development,
benchmark, and upstream example dependencies retain their own licenses and are
not necessarily part of the standard runtime package.

Models downloaded at runtime likewise have licenses independent of GenieX.
Retain each model's own accompanying license and notices.
